    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e4j7twu",
      "content": "<strong><br></br>4. Structure of a Typical Cell</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ii4nu7z",
      "content": "A typical cell consists of three main parts:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "l5ulb0u",
      "content": "1.Cell membrane"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "mktjnxn",
      "content": "2.Cytoplasm"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "6a3qitp",
      "content": "3.Nucleus"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3mdvpe7",
      "content": "<strong><br></br>5. Cell Organelles and Their Detailed Functions</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "8ol7ize",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Organelle</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Function</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Cell Membrane</p>",
            "<p>Selectively permeable membrane controlling entry and exit of substances.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Cell Wall</p>",
            "<p>Rigid outer layer present in plant cells made of cellulose.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Cytoplasm</p>",
            "<p>Jelly-like matrix containing organelles and site of metabolic reactions.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Nucleus</p>",
            "<p>Control center containing DNA and chromosomes.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mitochondria</p>",
            "<p>Powerhouse of the cell; produces ATP; contains its own DNA.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Ribosomes</p>",
            "<p>Site of protein synthesis.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Endoplasmic Reticulum</p>",
            "<p>Network for transport; RER synthesizes proteins, SER synthesizes lipids.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Golgi Apparatus</p>",
            "<p>Modifies, packages and secretes proteins.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Lysosomes</p>",
            "<p>Contain digestive enzymes; called suicide bags.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Plastids</p>",
            "<p>Present in plants; chloroplast performs photosynthesis.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Vacuole</p>",
            "<p>Storage of water, food and waste materials.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p4v5dv0",
      "content": "<strong>6. Difference Between Plant and Animal Cell</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "2h71ax9",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Feature</strong></p>",
