    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "bi93kic",
      "content": "<strong><br></br>19. Cell Communication</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gmcotwq",
      "content": "1.Cells communicate through chemical signals."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i906w5i",
      "content": "2. Hormones act as signaling molecules."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jt4hovg",
      "content": "3.Receptors present on cell membrane receive signals."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "tefsx77",
      "content": "<strong><br></br>20. Important Quick Revision Points </strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "stwa8i9",
      "content": "1.Fluid mosaic model explains plasma membrane structure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cp7rdoc",
      "content": "2. Centrioles help in spindle formation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "15vq55r",
      "content": "3. Crossing over occurs in Prophase I of meiosis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
